timeline.body:
Instead of forcing `jdk.scripting.nashorn` onto the module path we should make sure that the substitutions that fail without are written in a way so that they can handle `jdk.scripting.nashorn` to be missing.

I.e. Define a new `BooleanSupplier` that is only true when module `jdk.scripting.nashorn` is available and add it to the `@TargetClass` annotations `onlyWith`-attribute e.g.
```java
@TargetClass(className = "jdk.nashorn.api.scripting.ClassFilter", onlyWith = {JDK14OrEarlier.class, hasModuleNashorn.class})
public final class Target_jdk_nashorn_api_scripting_ClassFilter {
}
```
and
```java
@TargetClass(className = "jdk.nashorn.api.scripting.NashornScriptEngineFactory", onlyWith = {JDK14OrEarlier.class, hasModuleNashorn.class})
public final class Target_jdk_nashorn_api_scripting_NashornScriptEngineFactory {
...
}
```

