reply.body:
> I fail to see why we need this check since we know that nashorn is available in JDK <= 14 and we already check for that.
> What am I missing?

@zakkak The issue is similar to the fix needed in `getBuilderModulePath()`. The issue that this fixes is the failure of building the native image agent (i.e. building a module, not default classpath) via the `native-image-agent-library` macro. See failure in https://github.com/oracle/graal/issues/3778#issuecomment-917077931 For that build the `jdk.scripting.nashorn` module isn't explicitly on the module path, so the target class isn't found. You can simulate this behaviour on a JDK 11, say, with `--limit-modules=java.base` and you'd get a CNFE on the target class in question. Does that make sense?
